Z||000000||isthiswhereiputausername?||06-06-2001||11:39 AM||||I removed my rust causing sound insulation from my engine compartment.. but theres still some on my firewall.. Anyone ever try to replace this?  I wouldnt want to remove it completely because of road/engine noise but would like to get it replaced before its rusts anything..<P>I have a 2.8L with a thrush muffler of it so I definely need the deadening..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||TRL46202||09-11-2001||09:59 AM||||Did you ever get an answer to this??? email me..............||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||09-11-2001||11:30 AM||||I have heard of some people removing the sound proofing from the sides around the strut towers and reported an increase of road noise. They do say that it is easier to keep the engine compartment clean.<BR>I'm not sure about factory availability of replacement blankets.<BR>If it were me, I would leave the one on the fire wall in place.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroBUZZ||09-11-2001||12:43 PM||||I saw some that was completly sealed with a tin foil appearance.  That would keep the water out of the insulation.  The center section is safe because of the heat from the manifold (like the trunk 'firewall' which looks new while the sides are rotted away).  The alternative is to remove it and sound/heat proof the inside back wall of the passenger compartment.<BR>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000004||chester||09-11-2001||01:31 PM||||I found a product made by Thermo-Tec.  I'm going to reline my engine compartment with this material.  It is a sound reducing, heat reflective material.  I think you can get it in both self stick sheets and sheets that you use the plastic plugs to hold it in place like the original stuff. Here is a link to the manufactures web page (which appears to be down right now)and one to a distributor.  Hope this helps. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.thermotec.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.thermotec.com</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.stockcarproducts.com/insulat2.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.stockcarproducts.com/insulat2.htm</A> <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">   <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||6
